# local-mail provider credentials.
#
# Machine-wide override for the Google OAuth Desktop client supplied by a
# packaged Local Mail distribution. Source builds need this pair because they
# carry no distribution identity. One identity serves every Gmail account
# connected on this machine. The stored token records the concrete client id
# that minted it, so a later client-id change fails loudly and asks you to
# reconnect every account, instead of surfacing as Google's opaque invalid_grant.
# See docs/adr/0188-*.md for why the identity belongs to the distribution rather
# than to the Epicenter instance you selected.
#
# Provide these in your environment for the first connect or seed-token: an
# export, a local .env, or a secrets manager such as
# `infisical run --path=/apps/local-mail -- ...` if that is how you keep
# secrets.
#
# After the first successful connect or refresh, Local Mail caches the pair to a
# 0600 <data-dir>/provider.json. Later runs and other git worktrees on this
# machine read it from there with no per-worktree config.

GMAIL_CLIENT_ID=
GMAIL_CLIENT_SECRET=
